    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "27 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2026-08-12 23:47:00 EDT Expires: 2026-08-13 00:30:00 EDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building. Target Area: Orange At 1146 PM EDT, Doppler radar was tracking strong thunderstorms along a line extending from Woodridge to Thompsonville to near Rock Hill to near Hartwood. Movement was east at 30 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to outdoor objects is possible.\nLocations impacted include... Newburgh, Walden, Howells, Gardnertown, Montgomery, Otisville, Scotchtown, Orange Lake, Mechanicstown, Balmville, Maybrook, Pine Bush, Circleville, and Bullville.",
